---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = "What is a Webhook? A Complete Guide for Developers - WebhookCatch";
const description = "Learn what a webhook is, how it works, and how it differs from a traditional API. Read our comprehensive guide with examples.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is a webhook?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A webhook is an HTTP-based callback function that allows lightweight, event-driven communication between two APIs. It automatically sends data to a specified URL when a specific event occurs."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is a webhook different from an API?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "An API requires you to constantly poll or ask for data, whereas a webhook pushes data to you automatically as soon as an event happens."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />

  <Navbar />

  <main style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 100px 24px; color: var(--color-ink);">
    <h1 class="text-heading-1" style="margin-bottom: 24px; font-weight: 700;">What is a Webhook?</h1>
    <p class="text-body-lg" style="color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: 48px;">
      A webhook (also called a web callback or HTTP push API) is a way for an app to provide other applications with real-time information. Unlike traditional APIs where you have to poll for data frequently, a webhook delivers data to other applications as it happens.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">How does a webhook work?</h2>
    <p class="text-body" style="color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: 24px;">
      When an event occurs in the source application (like a new user signing up, or a payment succeeding), it triggers an HTTP request (usually a <code>POST</code> request) to a destination URL that you configure. This destination URL is known as the webhook endpoint.
    </p>
    <div style="background: var(--color-surface); padding: 24px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <code style="font-family: monospace; display: block; margin-bottom: 8px;">Event Happens ➔ Application ➔ HTTP POST ➔ Your Webhook Endpoint</code>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Common Use Cases</h2>
    <ul class="text-body" style="color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: 48px; padding-left: 20px;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;"><strong>Payment Gateways (Stripe, PayPal):</strong> Notifying your database when a subscription renews or a payment fails.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;"><strong>CI/CD & Source Control (GitHub, GitLab):</strong> Triggering an automated build pipeline when a developer pushes code.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;"><strong>Chat Apps (Slack, Discord):</strong> Sending an automated message to a channel when a specific event happens on your server.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-heading-2" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">How to test webhooks?</h2>
    <p class="text-body" style="color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: 24px;">
      When you are building an integration that relies on webhooks, you need a way to see exactly what payload the provider is sending you. Because webhooks are sent from a third-party server directly to a URL, you can't just view them in your browser network tab.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body" style="color: var(--color-body); margin-bottom: 48px;">
      That's where a Webhook Tester comes in. By using a tool like <a href="/">WebhookCatch</a>, you can instantly generate a unique URL, plug it into the third-party service, and watch the HTTP requests stream in.
    </p>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 64px; padding: 48px; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); border-radius: 12px;">
      <h3 class="text-heading-3" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Ready to test a webhook?</h3>
      <a href="/" class="btn-primary" style="text-decoration: none; display: inline-flex; justify-content: center;">Generate Free Webhook URL</a>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
